 table('7','Table07_Block_Length_Development','Training-only comparison used to select the block length.', ['Rank','Generator / block length',r'VS-1, 16 curves (dB$^2$)',r'VS-1, first 8 curves (dB$^2$)','Dates'],rows,r'Lower VS-1 is better. The saved development experiment uses five date-group folds within 2404 local training hours, with 16 realizations and an 8-realization stability check. It is separate from the final 32-realization evaluation in Tables~8--9. The 256-s block has the lowest recorded score; its advantage over 128 s is about 0.12\%, a small descriptive separation. IID and Gaussian AR(1) are development controls.', ['frozen_exports/block_selection.csv','methods/11_DYNAMICS_PLAN.md','methods/12_DYNAMICS_RESULTS.md'])
